{"name":"For the Love of Hue","hex":"#457e87","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"for","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Fore."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["Because."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/for"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"},{"term":"hue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color, or shade of color; tint; dye.","The characteristic related to the light frequency that appears in the color, for instance red, yellow, green, cyan, blue or magenta."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shout or cry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hue"}],"entries":[{"title":"For the Love","blocks":[{"text":"For the Love is the ninth studio album by American country music artist Tracy Lawrence. It was released on January 30, 2007, by Rocky Comfort Records. It debuted at #53 on the Billboard 200. Three singles were released from the album: \"Find Out Who Your Friends Are\" reached #1 on the Billboard Hot Country Songs chart and became Lawrence's first chart-topping song since \"Time Marches On\" in mid-1996. The album's second single, \"Til I Was a Daddy Too\", reached #32 on the same chart, which would be his final Top 40 Hit on that chart, \"You Can't Hide Redneck\" was released in October 2008 as the third single, peaking at #56 on the Billboard Hot Country Songs chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Forthelove.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/For_the_Love"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"},{"title":"Hue","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, hue is one of the properties of a color, defined in the CIECAM02 model as \"the degree to which a stimulus can be described as similar to or different from stimuli that are described as red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet\", within certain theories of color vision."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Colors-i54-ring.png/330px-Colors-i54-ring.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/1280px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg/500px-Columpio_Veracruz_059.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fraternal love (Prehispanic sculpture from 250 to 900 CE, of Huastec origin). Museum of Anthropology in Xalapa, Veracruz, Mexico","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColumpio_Veracruz_059.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg/500px-Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Gothaer_Liebespaar.jpg/500px